note """
The end-to-end fixture for an EMBEDDED SUBFLOW. Until this one the assembler's
end-to-end programs carried no `use` at all, which is half of why a signature-
carrying subflow could emit a wiring function reading an unbound `in` and reach a
shipped command: the goldens did not compile a `use` and the run fixtures did not
run one.

THE TOKEN IS REACHED ONLY THROUGH THE EMBEDDED BODY. Every datum passes the
subflow's branch on its way to the sink, so a `use` that generated but routed
nothing prints nothing. The count is three: the transport delivers two and the
host pushes the third through the exported ingest, so an ingest that is merely
typed leaves the flow one short.
"""

flow screening (Order) -> ok Order, bad Order
branch triage Interesting from in -> ok, bad

flow embedded
source ingest Feed()
transform count Count from ingest
use screen screening from count -> ok, bad
sink emit Report from ok
drop bad
